  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Qi Zai tells Qi He that the Heaven Surveying Five Xiangs were five publicly recognized rank eight Gu Immortal experts in Southern Border who collaborated and explored white heaven and black heaven together. Qi clan’s ancestor was one of them, Qi Xiang, and Qi clan cultivates qi path primarily because of him. Qi Zai names the five as Qi Xiang, Ni Xiang, Bai Xiang, Xue Xiang, and Chi Xiang.",
      "chapters": [
        1035
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qi_zai",
        "char_qi_he",
        "fac_heaven_surveying_five_xiangs",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_qi_clan",
        "char_ni_xiang",
        "char_xue_xiang",
        "char_chi_xiang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan assigns the Five Xiangs’ paths as qi, ice, blood, earth, and food respectively, with Qi Xiang on qi path. Qi clan Gu Immortals treat Qi Xiang true inheritance as their answer to Bai Xiang killer move at the Five Xiangs’ gatehouse. Fang Yuan judges Qi Xiang’s power his remaining obstacle there.",
      "chapters": [
        1637
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "paths-and-true-inheritance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Related inheritance detail sits on Qi Xiang true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "paths-and-true-inheritance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_qi_xiang_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Xiang was very strong in life. After he died, Qi Sea grotto-heaven remained without devouring any nine heavens fragment, so it still faced endless calamities and tribulations. His lifetime accumulation left over a million qi path dao marks. The Qi Sea heavenly spirit formed from Qi Xiang’s obsession fused with the grotto-heaven’s heavenly power.",
      "chapters": [
        1816
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qi-sea-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qi_sea_grotto_heaven",
        "char_qi_sea_ancestor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Xiang left the killer move unlimited qi sea, allowing Qi Xiang grotto-heaven’s heavenly spirit to pass myriad tribulations again and again after his death.",
      "chapters": [
        2052
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "killer-move-left-behind",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
